# Preserve Commented Code

When making changes in this project, **do not delete existing commented-out code** unless the user explicitly asks to remove it.

## Required behavior

- Keep existing `//`, `/* */`, `{/* */}`, and `#` comments that contain code, notes, or disabled implementations
- When refactoring or cleaning up, leave commented blocks in place
- You may add new comments, but do not remove old ones as part of routine edits
- If commented code blocks a required change, leave the comment and implement the change around it

## Allowed removal (only when the user explicitly requests it)

- The user asks to remove commented code, dead code, or clean up comments
- The user asks to delete a specific commented block by name or location

## Not allowed during normal edits

- Removing commented code to reduce file size
- Removing commented code as "cleanup" or "code quality" without being asked
- Replacing commented code with a note like "removed old implementation"

## Examples

```javascript
// ❌ Do not delete this during unrelated edits
// const legacyFetch = () => fetch('/old-endpoint');

// ✅ Leave it; make your change elsewhere
export function fetchData() {
  return fetch('/api/data');
}
```

If you believe commented code must be removed for correctness, **ask the user first** instead of deleting it.
